-- Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two, three power armors (printed 110-123): Lynx, Mantis, Med-Rec White Knight
-- 3 vehicle rows, with 43 locations and 12 weapon entries.
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration - it adds
-- rows, not schema.
--
--   node scripts/d1-apply.mjs --local apps/character-creator/db/~307-northern-gun-2-power-armor-e.sql
--
-- Written by scripts/vessel-sql.mjs from 1 worker file(s). Every value
-- is printable ASCII, every row cites its book, and a Main Body location
-- agrees with its vehicle's mdc_main_body.

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO vehicles (slug, name, system, vehicle_class, crew, passengers, speed_ground, speed_air, speed_water, dimensions, weight_tons, mdc_main_body, is_mega_damage, ar, cost, cost_note, description, source_book) VALUES
  ('ng-x112-lynx', 'Lynx Power Armor', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One.', NULL, 'Running: 50 mph (printed as 80 mph for the metric figure) at top speed, 25% of the normal fatigue rate; 10% at 35 mph (56 km) or less. Leaping: 15 ft (4.6 m) up or across unassisted, 25 ft (7.6 m) with the leg thrusters only, each +50% with a running start. VTOL leaps: the back thruster hurls it 200 ft (61 m) vertically or on a shallow slant, and higher still by rebounding off buildings, but once launched it can hardly stop or turn. Power Jumping Travel: 90 mph (144 km) in repeated 20-50 ft (6.1 to 15.2 m) bounds, halved over dense brush, deep mud or snow and other rough ground; crashing through woods gives -3 initiative, -3 Perception and -1 to strike, parry and dodge (not on open streets or rooftops).', 'None; it can hover only 1D4 melee actions before wobbling back down.', 'Cannot swim; jet thrusters drive it underwater at 12 mph (19 km/10.4 knots), or it walks the bottom at 5 mph (8 km/4.3 knots). Maximum depth 800 ft (244 m).', 'Man-sized: height 6-7.6 ft (1.8 to 2.3 m); width 2.4-3 ft (0.73 to 0.9 m); length 2-3 ft (0.6 to 0.9 m)', '465 lbs (209 kg)', 245, 1, NULL, 1200000, '2 million credits nuclear, 1.6 million Solid Oxide, 1.2 million electric battery; the lowest is stored. The Big Bang rifle comes with the suit and carries no separate price.', 'Model Type: NG-X112. Class: Urban Assault and Xiticix Fighter Power Armor. Designed by Tim Frates, Christopher Mangels and Chuck Tawlon as a hive raider (its prototype name was Bug Hunter 01) and partnered with the Cougar suit, which hunts down the Xiticix the Lynx knocks out of the air or flushes from side tunnels. Its back and leg thrusters let it shoot up and down vertical hive shafts, vault between tunnel levels and spring into the air to shoot or grapple flying bugs. One of Northern Gun''s most heavily armored suits, so its running speed is modest, but its jet-assisted bounding more than compensates. The same agility suits it to street fighting, riot control, commando raids, prison breaks and rescues: it bounds from roof to roof, rides elevator shafts, clears a staircase in a single jump, crashes in through upper windows and floats down from them carrying survivors, and many Upper Michigan fire brigades keep Lynx rescue units. Pilots often lope on all fours like a big cat. Only the Mantis is more nimble. It ships with NG''s new Universal Energy Link (UEL), an E-Clip on a cable to the suit''s power supply that gives any E-Clip weapon unlimited shots. Cat-like landings: thrusters slow falls of up to 800 ft (244 m) safely, people carried in its arms included; from 800 to 1,200 ft (366 m) roll 1D20, on 1-10 the suit takes 1D4x10 M.D. and the pilot loses 1D4 melee actions, on 11-20 no harm; higher drops do 3D4x10 M.D. to the suit, 1D4x10 S.D.C./Hit Points to the wearer and stun him 1D4 melee rounds. Special bonuses: +1 on initiative, +1 to strike when leaping to grab, tackle or slash, +2 to dodge while running or power jumping, +1 to roll with impact. Robot P.S. 28. Cargo: a small compartment in each shoulder (a canteen or three grenades) plus belts and pouches. Power: nuclear, 12 year average life; Solid Oxide and electric battery versions are sold. Any handheld weapon may be used, energy weapons by preference since the UEL feeds them; a side arm, Vibro-Blade and grenade reloads ride on one or two belts. UEL (2, one under plating in each forearm): powers a weapon of up to 1D6x10 M.D. a blast; a breaker shuts off anything stronger. Hand to hand per Basic or Elite Ground-Based Power Armor Training (Rifts Ultimate Edition p.351-352): restrained punch 1D4 M.D., full punch 1D6, power punch 2D6 (two attacks), kick 2D4, leap kick 2D8 (two attacks). Features beyond the standard: a dash-cam style helmet camera on top of the head and a concealed gun camera (96 hours of video, 4,000 stills); an LED head lamp in the forehead (500 ft/152 m); and passive nightvision (2,000 ft/610 m), useless in total darkness. Losing one thruster cuts leaping speed and distance by 30%, losing both by 60% and ends underwater jet travel.', 'Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two p.110-113'),
  ('ng-x39-mantis', 'Mantis Power Armor', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One.', NULL, 'Running: 50 mph (printed as 80 mph for the metric figure) at top speed, 25% of the normal fatigue rate; 10% at 35 mph (56 km) or less. Leaping: 15 ft (4.6 m) up or across unassisted, 30 ft (9.1 m) with the leg thrusters only (45 ft/13.7 m running). VTOL leaps: the back jets throw it 200 ft (61 m) up or forward, and unlike the Lynx it can steer, slow or stop in mid-leap, though it cannot rebound off buildings; it climbs with its hands or blades instead. Power Jumping Travel: 90 mph (144 km) in 20-50 ft (6.1 to 15.2 m) bounds, halved in dense brush, mud, snow or broken ground; crashing through woods gives -3 initiative, -3 Perception and -1 to strike, parry and dodge (not on open streets or rooftops).', 'None; it can hover only 1D4 melee actions before drifting down.', 'Cannot swim; jet thrusters drive it underwater at up to 12 mph (19 km/10.4 knots), or it walks the bottom at 6 mph (9.6 km/5 knots). Maximum depth 800 ft (244 m).', 'Man-sized: height 6-7.6 ft (1.8 to 2.3 m); width 2.4-3 ft (0.73 to 0.9 m); length 3 ft (0.9 m)', '485 lbs (218 kg)', 195, 1, NULL, 1400000, '2.3 million credits nuclear, 1.9 million Solid Oxide, 1.4 million electric battery; the lowest is stored.', 'Model Type: NG-X39. Class: Armored Infantry Assault Suit with Xiticix-fighting capabilities. A robot killer from the team of Ben Bonds, Chris Curcio, Sam Beeda and Harlan Oscwelt, styled after the praying mantis. Its main weapons are two big double-edged scythe blades on the forearms, best wielded like paired samurai swords by a pilot with Hand to Hand: Martial Arts; folded back along the forearm they still stab rearward, parry, and snap out to counter. Built to raid Xiticix hives, to cripple giant robots, magic Automatons, Iron Juggernauts, tanks and dreadnaughts, to board ships and cut through hulls, and for close combat in general; silver-plated blades and a few anti-demon weapons make it useful against the supernatural. Doctrine is to whittle a big machine down piece by piece rather than seek a kill: first sensors, then communications, then weapons (cables and UEL cords first, then the heaviest guns), then locomotion (wings and thrusters, wheels, treads and legs, rudders and props), then leave it for others and move to the next target, ideally two or three Mantises tag-teaming one target like lions on big game. Never stand toe to toe with a giant robot. Each suit ships with a manual of moves and an eight hour training video. Many pilots keep a samurai-like code and let a beaten foe flee or surrender. Its weakness is a lack of medium and long range weapons. Popular with Juicers, Crazies, Cyborgs, Cyber-Knights and swordsmen and a Robodome crowd favorite, it was among NG''s ten best sellers in 109 P.A.; packs of Mantises in bandit and pirate hands raiding ships and caravans have made sales controversial, but NG still sells to anyone who pays. Cat-like landings: falls up to 800 ft (244 m) are safe, passengers in its arms included; from 800 to 1,200 ft (366 m) roll 1D20, on 1-10 the suit takes 1D4x10 M.D. and the pilot loses 1D4 melee actions, on 11-20 no harm; higher drops do 3D4x10 M.D. to the suit, 1D4x10 S.D.C./Hit Points to the wearer and stun him 1D4 melee rounds. Special bonuses: +2 to parry, +2 to automatic dodge, +1 to disarm, +1 to pull punch. Robot P.S. 30. Cargo: belt pouches only; it cannot wear a backpack. Power: nuclear, 12 year average life; Solid Oxide and electric battery versions are sold. Hand to hand (blunt attacks) per Basic or Elite Ground-Based Power Armor Training (Rifts Ultimate Edition p.351-352): restrained punch 1D4 M.D., full punch 1D6, power punch 2D6 (two attacks), kick 2D4, leap kick 2D8 (two attacks). Features beyond the standard: helmet multi-optics with passive nightvision and infrared (1,600 ft/488 m) and thermal optics (1,000 ft/305 m); two temple searchlights, one visible and one infrared, that follow the gaze to 200 ft (61 m) and tilt 30 degrees (the features text gives them 5 M.D.C., the location table 10 each); and a mouthpiece loudspeaker with language translator and 20-voice modulator. Each lost thruster cuts thruster-assisted leaping and power jumping by 20%; losing all four cuts speed and distance by 60% and ends underwater jet travel.', 'Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two p.114-118'),
  ('ng-mru876-med-rec-white-knight', 'Med-Rec "White Knight" Power Armor', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One.', NULL, 'Running: 50 mph (80 km) maximum, 20% of the normal fatigue rate. Leaping: 10 ft (3 m) high or across, half again as far after a run; from a standstill the jets can carry it 16 ft (4.9 m) high and 160 ft (48.8 m) across.', 'Limited flight on the standard MEDVAC jet pack: 70 mph (112 km), ceiling 900 ft (274 m). Range is unlimited when the pack draws on the suit''s nuclear or Solid Oxide supply through its back connector; on its reserve electric battery, 500 miles (800 km) or 42 hours, whichever comes first. The pack can be detached to squeeze into tight places.', 'Swims 10 mph (16 km) or walks the bottom at 5 mph (8 km/4.3 knots). The jet pack is useless submerged and must dry for 1D4+4 hours before flying. Maximum depth 800 ft (244 m).', 'Man-sized, to the buyer''s size: height 6-8 ft (1.8 to 2.4 m); width 2.5-3.4 ft (0.76 to 1 m); length 2.5 ft (0.76 m)', '345 lbs (155 kg)', 180, 1, NULL, 1000000, '1.9 million credits nuclear, 1.5 million Solid Oxide, 1 million electric battery; the lowest is stored. The price covers the jet pack, the grenade launcher and all listed medical gear; replacement nano-robot systems, equipment and medicine cost extra. Replacement Med-EVAC markers are 200 each (gear row ng-mru876-med-evac-marker). The six nano-robot systems it carries already have catalog rows, and this book''s prices match them: IRMSS 42,000 a kit, IROU Breather 50,000, IRVT Seekers 80,000, RAU Cleaners 50,000 a pair, RMK Knitter 24,000, RSU Sleepers 100,000 a set of four.', 'Model Type: NG-MRU876. Class: Strategic Medical and Rescue Military Exoskeleton. A mobile medic suit from the Gleba design team (MacKenzie Coker, Bruce Curry, Michael Estrada and Arlo Chenstawl), meant to work alongside military and civilian rescue services, field hospitals and the MMB-01 Big Papa and MMB-02 Junior Mobile Medical Robots, being smaller and more agile than either. Best worn by a Medical Doctor or a Paramedic with some science, but firefighters and first responders trained in Firefighting, Demolitions, Mining, Excavation, Rope Works or Jury-Rig use it too; its wearers pull people out of battlefields, fires, collapsed buildings and mudslides, hence the nickname. It carries little in the way of weapons. Patient readings go to a corner of the HUD or are relayed by wireless to an MMB, hospital, clinic or base, and an MMB''s crew can share sensor data and triage with the suit, so a White Knight extends a medical robot''s reach. Back thrusters, apparently borrowed from the Triax Terrain Hopper, make it quick like the Lynx and Mantis. Each lower leg compartment is a full medical kit of surgical tools, bandages, sutures, loaded syringes (antibiotics, painkillers and the like) and nano-robot systems. Robot P.S. 26; the Jaws of Life has Robot P.S. 40. Cargo: none. Power: an NGMV4 micro-nuclear core lasting 4 years; Solid Oxide and electric battery models are also priced. Handheld weapons: small energy pistols are advised, since the forearm gear rules out rifles and heavy arms, and a medic is usually too busy to fight. UEL (2, one in an armored compartment in each forearm): powers medical gear or a weapon of up to 1D6x10 M.D. a blast; a breaker cuts off anything stronger. Hand to hand per Basic or Elite Ground-Based Power Armor Training (Rifts Ultimate Edition p.351-352): restrained punch 1D4 M.D., full punch 1D6, Jaws of Life hand punch or crush 2D4, power punch 2D6 (two attacks), kick 2D4, leap kick 2D8 (two attacks). Medical systems: a Diagnostic Computer and Medical Scanner filling the left forearm that, with a wireless finger clamp and sensor pads, tracks breathing, pulse, blood pressure, blood sugar and temperature, works as an EKG and EEG, and with a slow pass of a wand does the work of a CAT scan in 1D4+1 minutes, giving Body Fixers, Paramedics and Medical Doctors +10% to diagnose and +5% on related Medical skills. Features beyond the standard: voice control of the suit, computer and medical systems; a chest housing that drops open on a defibrillator and the portable Bio-Lab and Bio-Scan (Rifts Ultimate Edition p.263); 12 Med-EVAC markers, small red cards with a white cross that clip to a casualty or stretcher and ping on a frequency rescuers recognize, different from the Forester''s trail markers (one mile/1.6 km for 240 hours); an LED light (40 ft/12.2 m) and a small camera on each hand for peering into rubble; a forehead lamp (100 ft/30.5 m); multi-optics with passive nightvision and infrared (1,600 ft/488 m), ultraviolet (400 ft/122 m), a x20 macro camera and a recorder of 100 hours and 4,000 stills; a thermal imager (800 ft/244 m) for finding people under debris or in smoke; an infrared spotlight on the right shoulder (300 ft/91.4 m) for searching without showing a light; and a proximity alarm fed by small cameras on the helmet, shoulders, chest and back that calls out anything within 100 ft (30.5 m) and shows it on request until told it is friendly. It comes with at least six of each nano-robot medical system: IRMSS robot surgeons, the IROU Breather, IRVT Seekers, RAU Cleaners, RMK Knitter and RSU Sleepers, priced in their own catalog rows. Destroying the jet pack ends all flight.', 'Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two p.119-123');

